# ⛔ THE CLASS, NOT ONE NAME. This line was exactly `.venv` -- which matches one
# directory and nothing else. Measured 08/26: `.venv.old` sat beside it,
# UNIGNORED, 1.2 GB across 7,215 files, and `git add -A` in this PUBLIC repo
# would have staged every one of them. A rule naming a single instance READS as
# covering the class, and the sibling it does not cover is invisible in review
# because .gitignore is the file nobody re-derives.
# Verified before broadening: 0 tracked files match `.venv*`, so this ignores
# nothing that is currently in the index.
.venv
.venv*/
*.lock
bazel*
[xyz]

# Local editor / agent scratch
examples
transcript/
.claude
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/projects/
.claude/.credentials.json

# OCaml / dune build artifacts that sometimes leak into the repo root
*.cmi
*.cmx
*.o

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editor backup / scratch files (emacs backups + auto-saves + locks, vim swap)
# (\# escapes the leading '#' so the pattern is not read as a comment)
*~
\#*\#
.\#*
*.sw[a-p]
.*.sw[a-p]

# macOS Finder metadata (do not rely on a contributor's global gitignore)
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Scratch images (e.g. article/figures/**/x.png)
x.png

# Screenshot output from capture.sh (capture.sh <AppName> screenshot.png)
screenshot.png

# NOTE: workspace/workspace.json is COMMITTED. Regenerate with:
#   python -m workspace_interpreter.compile workspace/ workspace/workspace.json
# CI enforces freshness; see scripts/check_workspace_json.sh.

# The geometry checkers' EXECUTED-COUNT account, written by
# `cross_language_algorithms.py --checker-report` and read back by
# `check_geometry_checkers.py --reconcile`. A PER-RUN artefact, never a fact
# about the tree: committed, it would sit in every checkout and let the
# reconcile step pass on a run where the step that WRITES it had been deleted.
# check_geometry_checkers.py asserts both halves -- that this entry exists,
# and that the file it reads is untracked.
checker-report.json

# Captured cargo-test streams from the native backend lanes (windows-native,
# native-ffi). The lane guard reads them; nothing tracks them.
native-lane.log
ffi-lane.log

# S-B spike build output (prototypes/sb_winui). The ffi_spike's bin/obj are
# already in the tree; these are not, and a WinUI restore drags in ~200MB.
prototypes/sb_winui/bin/
prototypes/sb_winui/obj/
# GENERALISED 2026-08-28. The two lines above named ONE prototype, so building a
# SIBLING prototype (sc_panel, on the S-C branches) left its bin/ and obj/
# untracked-but-unignored -- and untracked files survive a checkout, so they
# followed me onto this branch and I swept 3,380 lines of NuGet asset json into a
# commit. #19 had already had to untrack the same outputs once ("SCC1: untrack
# the build outputs I swept in with the report"), which is the tell: a rule
# written per-directory gets re-broken by the next directory. Glob the class.
prototypes/*/bin/
prototypes/*/obj/
prototypes/sb_winui/sb-verify.png
